         punched out via even-odd, not line art: a status-bar icon is an alpha mask a few
         pixels across, and two thin concentric strokes turn to mush there while the mass
         reads instantly. Android tints it; only the alpha survives.
         Same drawing as branding/glyph-shield-keeper.svg and the macOS tray glyph —
         keep the path data in sync.
         NOTE: android:fillType="evenOdd" needs API 24; on 22/23 the keyhole fills in and
         the glyph degrades to a plain shield. -->
